/E (The 64 hexagrams are a primitive, six-digit binary system. By playing the game 'Don't Tap the White Tile', where the user must tap the black tiles \(1 / Yang\) and avoid the white tiles \(0 / Yin\), the audience visually translate their inputs into one of the 64 ancient hexagramsis. And they need to navigate the physical exhibition space, hunting through the 64 glowing lightbox columns to find their specific analysis.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [12]
